I pushed out an RFC for a long-overdue update of the m68k defconfig
files to my defconfig branch:
https://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/geert/linux-m68k.git/commit/?h=defconfig&id=417ed3fbd7bcc4e909421d35984947d6e45009bb

This RFC updates the defconfigs to mainline v3.9. I.e. this does not include
EtherNEC/EtherNAT/NetUSBee, so I don't have to care (yet) about the
CONFIG_USB can of worms ;-)

Michael: I'm definitely interested in a list of options to enable USB
support for
atari_defconfig, without dragging in the whole kitchen sink.
Do we also want this in multi_defconfig, which is currently the superset of
all (non-sun3) defconfigs? Or should USB be limited to atari_defconfig?

Note that these are all "reduced" defconfigs, as generated by "make
savedefconfig". I.e. for a proper view, you want to run "make xxx_defconfig"
and inspect the resulting .config file.

The non-m68k-specific settings should be the same for all defconfig files.
